! Example 1 : single mesh case.
! Study input file:
!   - Why do we set RADIATION=F?
!   - What are we requesting in SLICEs, and Boundary SLICEs?
!   - Look at the 2 &DEVC lines at the end, what are we requesting to output?
!
! Part a:
! Run case. Open Smokeview:
!   - Load up Temperature Slice, what do we get? Divergence? Density?
!   - Load up Velocity Error Boundary slice. What do we have?
! Open the run's device file (results/Example_1_FFT_devc.csv):
!   - how do VDOT_IN and VDOT_OUT compare at every time step?
! Comment (i.e with a #)
!            &PRES SOLVER='FFT'/
! Uncomment
!           #&PRES VELOCITY_TOLERANCE=0.001, MAX_PRESSURE_ITERATIONS=50/
! and rerun with ./run.sh FFT_tight. Is the velocity error reduced in smokeview?
! What about volume flows in and out?
!
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  

&HEAD CHID='Example_1_FFT', TITLE='Flow around confined Obstacle.' /

&MESH IJK=32,16,16, XB=0.,3.2,-0.8,0.8,-0.8,0.8 /
&TIME T_END=8. /
&RADI RADIATION=.FALSE. /
&MISC STRATIFICATION=F/

! Exactly one of the four &PRES lines below is active. To switch solver, comment
! the current one with a # and uncomment another, then pass the matching name to
! run.sh. It reads the VARIANT tags below and refuses to run if the two disagree,
! so a run can never be labelled with a solver it did not use.
! FFT is the default solver, so the first line only makes it explicit.
&PRES SOLVER='FFT' /                                         ! VARIANT=FFT
#&PRES VELOCITY_TOLERANCE=0.001, MAX_PRESSURE_ITERATIONS=50/ ! VARIANT=FFT_tight
#&PRES SOLVER='ULMAT', CHECK_POISSON=T/                      ! VARIANT=ULMAT        (PARDISO)
#&PRES SOLVER='ULMAT HYPRE', CHECK_POISSON=T/                ! VARIANT=ULMAT_HYPRE

! Define Surface BCs:
&SURF ID='WALLS', COLOR='GRAY', ADIABATIC=T, DEFAULT=T /
&SURF ID='INLET', COLOR='RED', VEL=-2.5 /

! We leave a door in x=3.2 m OPEN:
&VENT XB=3.2,3.2,-0.3,0.3,-0.8,0.6, SURF_ID='OPEN' /
&VENT MB='XMIN', SURF_ID='INLET' /

! Place an Obstable in the middle:
&OBST XB=1.5,1.7,-0.8,0.8,-0.8,0.4 /

! Define output:
! Slices:
&SLCF PBY=0, QUANTITY='VELOCITY', VECTOR=T /
&SLCF PBY=0, QUANTITY='DIVERGENCE', CELL_CENTERED=T /
&SLCF PBY=0, QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', CELL_CENTERED=T /
&SLCF PBY=0, QUANTITY='DENSITY', CELL_CENTERED=T /

! Boundary slices:
&BNDF QUANTITY='VELOCITY ERROR' /

! Devices:
! Volume flow into domain:
&DEVC ID='VDOT_IN', XB=-0.1,0.1,-0.8,0.8,-0.8,0.8, QUANTITY='NORMAL VELOCITY', SURF_ID='INLET', STATISTICS='SURFACE INTEGRAL', TIME_AVERAGED=F/

! Volume flow out of domain (OPEN boundary):
&DEVC ID='VDOT_OUT', XB=3.1,3.3,-0.3,0.3,-0.8,0.6, QUANTITY='NORMAL VELOCITY', SURF_ID='OPEN', STATISTICS='SURFACE INTEGRAL', TIME_AVERAGED=F/

&DUMP SIG_FIGS=15/

&TAIL /
